own returns. PREDICTED BEFORE THIS RUN (EDGE.md 31c at 0ac7674, the
count finding at 773a35f): surrogates WILL find setups -- re-basing
does not flatten close-to-close returns the way it flattened the
open-vs-prior-close gap in slice 49 -- but they will schedule about
ONE trade each, because a state signal's flags form one contiguous
run and simulate_schedule takes one entry per run. One trade is far
below the 20-trade floor, so surrogates will be INCOMPLETE and
clause (c) will fail. That is a construction mismatch, NOT evidence
about instrument bias.

